From 1dca50edf28521880961df561737af292d69e1cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:40:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] namec: the error handler frees e.off before nexterror too

namec's handler frees e.name and e.elems, and for an error after
e.nerror elements builds the message from e.off and frees it; with
e.nerror 0 it goes on to nexterror() first, and e.off (parsename's
smalloc) leaked, for every error with e.nerror 0: a create of /, an
open of /, . or a bare #x that the device refuses, a walk whose start
is not a directory.  e.off is nil or a live allocation there, and
nothing after the nexterror reads or frees it.  Found reviewing the
namec volatile patch (2026-11-27); compiled, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/src/9/port/chan.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/src/9/port/chan.c b/sys/src/9/port/chan.c
index de49d31f8..333823127 100644
--- a/sys/src/9/port/chan.c
+++ b/sys/src/9/port/chan.c
@@ -1394,8 +1394,10 @@ namec(char *aname, int amode, int omode, ulong perm)
 		/*
 		 * Prepare nice error, showing first e.nerror elements of name.
 		 */
-		if(e.nerror == 0)
+		if(e.nerror == 0){
+			free(e.off);
 			nexterror();
+		}
 		if(e.off[e.nerror]==0)
 			print("nerror=%d but off=%d\n",
 				e.nerror, e.off[e.nerror]);
